  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IFPIM H&#xe5;llbar medieutveckling i &#xd6;stP 2024-2028</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IFPIM Sustainable media 2024-2028 EE - Sustainable media development  2023-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Media development in the Eastern Partnership Region in order to increase the sustainability of independent MSMEs so they can offer access to information and employment. The fund offers grants based on a call off process that independent media organizations can be eligible.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Medieutveckling i den &#xd6;stliga Partnerskapsregionen med syfte att &#xf6;ka h&#xe5;llbarheten f&#xf6;r oberoende micro/sm&#xe5;/medelstora medieorganisationer s&#xe5; att de kan bidra med information samt erbjuda arbetstillf&#xe4;llen. Fonden utlyser kravst&#xe4;llda g&#xe5;vost&#xf6;d regelbundet som oberoende medieorganisationer kan s&#xf6;ka.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The planned outcomes of the proposed intervention

OUTCOME 1: A diverse cohort of public interest media outlets are provided with flexible core funding;

OUTCOME 2: Relevant and timely technical support to media outlets who request it;

OUTCOME 3: Innovations that unlock new, long term sources of funding for public interest media are developed;

OUTCOME 4: Learnings and promising solutions identified and shared;

OUTCOME 5: Supported media collectively publish public interest content that meets core professional standards across the selected public interest dimensions. Core support enables grantees to improve editorial standards overall, including gender sensitive reporting and the amplification of womens and marginalized voices;

OUTCOME 6: Supported media are sustained and continue to have the means to inform the public;

OUTCOME 7: Supported media improve their economic resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
